<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 30 November, from 883 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghdad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">883 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,143 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abu al-Abbas holds a victory parade in Baghdad after the Zanj Rebellion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Abu al-Abbas, the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutadid">al-Mu'tadid</a>, held a victory parade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanj-rebellion">Zanj Rebellion</a>. The revolt in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, led by Ali ibn Muhammad and involving enslaved and freed Africans, had ended with the fall of al-Mukhtarah in August.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanj-rebellion">Zanj Rebellion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1016">1016 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,010 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edmund Ironside dies, leaving Cnut king of all England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edmund II died weeks after agreeing to divide <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> with the Danish king Cnut. Cnut became sole king, later also ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in a North Sea empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1667">1667 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">359 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jonathan Swift is born in Dublin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jonathan Swift, later Dean of St Patrick's Cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, was born. His Gulliver's Travels and A Modest Proposal made him one of the great satirists in English.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1700">1700 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">326 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles XII's Swedish troops rout the Russian army at Narva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 8,000 Swedish troops under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII</a> routed a Russian army three to four times their size that was besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a>, early in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>. The defeat prompted Peter I's reforms, which gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> a standing professional army.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-narva-1700">Battle of Narva (1700)</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII of Sweden</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Clemens, later Mark Twain, is born</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-twain">Samuel Langhorne Clemens</a> was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, Missouri. As Mark Twain he wrote The Adventures of Tom Sawyer and Adventures of Huckleberry Finn, drawing on his boyhood on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1872">1872 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">154 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scotland and England play the first international football match</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> drew 0-0 at Hamilton Crescent in Partick, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>, before about 4,000 spectators. It is recognised by FIFA as the first official international football match.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union invades Finland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winter-war">Winter War</a>. Fierce Finnish resistance inflicted heavy losses before Finland ceded territory in March 1940, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>'s poor showing was noted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1995">1995 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bill Clinton becomes the first US president to visit Northern Ireland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bill Clinton addressed crowds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belfast">Belfast</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derry">Derry</a> in support of the peace process. The visit added momentum to the talks that produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/good-friday-agreement">Good Friday Agreement</a> in 1998.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 30 November <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-duke-of-berry"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-duke-of-berry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John, Duke of Berry</span><span class="tp">1340–1416</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/casimir-iv-jagiellon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/casimir-iv-jagiellon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Casimir IV Jagiellon</span><span class="tp">1427–1492</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andrea-doria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andrea-doria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andrea Doria</span><span class="tp">1466–1560</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andrea-palladio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andrea-palladio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andrea Palladio</span><span class="tp">1508–1580</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mark-twain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mark-twain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mark Twain</span><span class="tp">1835–1910</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andres-bonifacio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andres-bonifacio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andrés Bonifacio</span><span class="tp">1863–1897</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/winston-churchill.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Winston Churchill</span><span class="tp">1874–1965</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 30 November <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edmund-ironside"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edmund-ironside.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edmund Ironside</span><span class="tp">c. 990–1016</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nanda-bayin"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Nanda Bayin</span><span class="tp">1535–1600</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cecil-calvert"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cecil-calvert.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cecil Calvert, 2nd Baron Baltimore</span><span class="tp">1605–1675</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ahmadou-ahidjo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ahmadou-ahidjo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ahmadou Ahidjo</span><span class="tp">1924–1989</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jiang-zemin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jiang-zemin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jiang Zemin</span><span class="tp">1926–2022</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
